UPDATE companies SET description='EPE Components operates from Salem, Massachusetts, where it serves as a specialized intermediary for excess and obsolete electronic inventory. The company focuses on helping original equipment manufacturers, electronics manufacturing services providers, and global supply chains convert idle component stock into working capital through structured resale and recovery programs.

Its service lines include excess inventory recovery via consignment or buyout, secure authorized remarketing to protect brand integrity, ESG circular reporting with data-backed sustainability metrics, and lifecycle obsolescence management to maintain supply continuity. Quality assurance is anchored by an AS9120B:2016 and ISO 9001:2015 certified management system, supplemented by ISO 14001 and ISO 45001 certifications. Inspection and testing capabilities cover documentation review, packaging verification, external visual inspection, remarking and resurfacing tests (scrape and solvent), X-ray inspection using an X6600/X6600B microfocus system, solderability testing on a MUST System 3 platform, decapsulation via a JetEtch chemical system, and high-magnification microscopy on a Keyence instrument (20–6000×). The company also maintains AS6081 compliance for counterfeit detection.

EPE''s customer base spans automotive, aviation/military, and medical sectors. In automotive, commodity managers monitor lead-time and obsolescence issues for components from suppliers such as NVIDIA, Intel, NXP, Infineon, Texas Instruments, Renesas, Bosch, Onsemi, and STMicroelectronics. Aviation and military clients rely on the firm''s AS9120 certification and use of DOD-certified test facilities when required. Medical customers receive semiconductors and LCDs sourced through a strict vendor screening process.

The company emphasizes transparent recovery processes, global buyer access to maximize pricing, and consignment strategies that it says often outperform traditional liquidation. Its quality program is built around rigorous incoming and outgoing inspection, detailed test reporting, and traceability documentation.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001','ISO 45001','AS9120B:2016','AS6081 compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Excess inventory recovery (consignment and buyout)", "Secure authorized remarketing", "ESG circular reporting", "Lifecycle obsolescence management", "Documentation inspection (part number, date code, CoC, country of origin, lot identification)", "Packaging inspection (condition, manufacturer packing, ESD/MSL compliance, bar codes)", "External visual inspection (body, markings, terminals, mechanical dimensions vs. datasheet)", "Remarking/resurfacing testing (scrape test, solvent test)", "X-ray inspection (X6600/X6600B microfocus system)", "Solderability testing (MUST System 3)", "Decapsulation (JetEtch chemical system)", "High-magnification microscopy (Keyence, 20\u20136000\u00d7)", "Counterfeit detection (AS6081 compliant)", "Inventory assessment and valuation", "Global resale and distribution", "Supply chain risk management"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aviation/Military", "Medical"], "materials": ["Semiconductors", "LCDs", "Electronic components"], "equipment": ["XRAY Machine X6600/X6600B", "MUST System 3 solderability tester", "JetEtch decapsulation system", "Keyence microscope (20\u20136000\u00d7)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Salem, Massachusetts -> db", "Business model: excess/obsolete electronic component resale and recovery for OEMs, EMS, global supply chains -> /", "Proprietary ClearView platform for tracking quotes, sales, balances, recovery performance -> /", "Service lines: excess inventory recovery (consignment/buyout), secure authorized remarketing, ESG circular reporting, lifecycle obsolescence management -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 14001, ISO 45001, AS9120 -> /", "Quality management: AS9120B:2016, ISO 9001:2015 -> /quality", "AS6081 compliant (soon to be certified) for counterfeit detection -> /quality", "Inspection processes: documentation, packaging, external visual, remarking/resurfacing testing -> /quality", "Testing equipment: XRAY Machine X6600/X6600B, MUST System 3 solderability tester, JetEtch decapsulation system, Keyence microscope -> /quality", "Industries served: Automotive (with named component suppliers), Aviation/Military, Medical -> /quality", "Automotive component suppliers: NVIDIA, Intel, NXP, Infineon, TI, Renesas, Bosch, On Semi, ST Microelectronics -> /quality", "Aviation/military: DOD-certified test facilities used when required -> /quality", "Medical: strict vendor screening for semiconductors and LCDs -> /quality"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "EPE helps OEMs, EMS providers, and global supply chains recover value from excess, obsolete, and slow-moving electronic components through transparent resale and inventory recovery programs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='epecomponents-electronic-parts-exchange' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ES Solar is headquartered in Layton, Utah, and was founded in 2010.

The company provides end-to-end solar solutions, handling design, permitting, installation, and ongoing service in-house. It has completed more than 15,000 installations across Utah, Nevada, California, Idaho, and Texas, serving both residential and commercial customers. Its service division performs an 8-point system check and monitoring for systems installed by ES Solar or other providers.

ES Solar works primarily with homeowners and business owners seeking to reduce energy costs and gain independence from the grid. Residential projects include rooftop solar and battery backup, while commercial installations help businesses lower operating expenses. The company also offers flexible financing structures such as cash purchase, prepaid leases, power purchase agreements, and loans.

