UPDATE companies SET description='Eartec Co Inc has been based in Narragansett, Rhode Island since its founding in 1961. Originally operating as the Eartec/Porta Phone Company, the business began by supplying state-of-the-art headset communications to a multitude of industries around the globe.

The company designs and manufactures a range of wireless headset communication systems, including the UltraLITE and UltraLITE PRO16 full-duplex intercom series, the Blackmagic Interface for wired intercom integration, the SCRAMBLER Plus two-way radio line, and the E-Pak digital wireless platform. It also offers the Global Connect IP-based communication link and the TCS Wired industrial-grade intercom. Eartec serves as the sole source repair center for its own brands in the United States and sells both direct and through authorized dealers.

Eartec’s systems are used in broadcast and stage production, commercial drone operations, equestrian instruction, marine captain-to-crew communication, radio-controlled racing, restaurant and food-service environments, sailing, non-commercial cafeteria settings, and industrial jobsites where wireless equipment is restricted or interference is a concern. Customers include production crews, drone pilots, riding instructors, vessel captains, RC racers, restaurant staff, sailors, and industrial teams.

The company emphasizes customer service as its top priority, highlighting real-person support, fast shipping (typically 1–3 business days), and a repair infrastructure that covers post-warranty assistance. Its wireless products employ frequency-hopping technology to evade interference, encrypted signals for privacy, and sufficient power to penetrate concrete and steel, all packaged in affordable midweight headsets.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wireless headset communication system design and manufacturing", "Full-duplex wireless intercom systems (DECT, frequency-hopping)", "Wired intercom interface integration (Blackmagic, TCS Wired)", "Two-way radio systems (simplex, push-to-talk, 500mW output)", "Digital wireless systems (E-Pak)", "Global IP-based communication (Global Connect)", "Repair and service for own brands", "Direct sales and authorized dealer distribution"], "industries": ["Broadcast & stage communications", "Commercial UAS (drone)", "Equestrian instruction", "Marine (captain to crew)", "Radio controlled racing", "Restaurant & food service", "Sailing", "Non-commercial food service (cafeteria)", "Industrial (light industrial)", "Jobsites with wireless restrictions"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1-3 business days for order shipping", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customer service prioritized with real-person support", "Sole source repair center for own brands in the USA", "Orders typically ship within 1\u20133 business days", "Frequency-hopping technology to evade interference", "Encrypted signals and concrete/steel penetration"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1961 -> db", "Headquarters Narragansett, RI -> db, /about", "Products: UltraLITE, UltraLITE PRO16, Blackmagic Interface, SCRAMBLER Plus, TCS Wired, E-Pak, Global Connect -> /", "Industries served: broadcast, drone, equestrian, marine, RC racing, restaurant, sailing, cafeteria, industrial -> /", "Sole source repair center for own brands 