UPDATE companies SET description='East Coast Metal Systems, Inc. (ECMS) operates from Triadelphia, West Virginia, where it runs a 60,000-square-foot fabrication facility. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but describes itself as having decades of experience in architectural metal and exterior envelope systems.

ECMS provides full-service fabrication for engineered architectural metal and exterior envelope systems, guiding projects from pre-construction through installation. Its capabilities include pre-construction services, 3D laser scanning, metal panel fabrication, custom fabrication, field supervision and installation, corporate identity programs, and historic restoration. The facility produces a range of proprietary systems: the EC-100 and EC-150 wet joint MCM systems, EC-200 and EC-250 dry joint MCM systems, EC-300 formed plate rainscreen system, EC Edge 1000 gravel stop system, and the OVERLY Panel Systems line of architectural metal wall and roof systems. Materials processed include metal composite material (MCM) with PE/FR cores, aluminum, copper, steel, stainless steel, and galvanized steel in various thicknesses.

Completed projects include the University of South Carolina Upstate Library, Westchester Medical Center in Valhalla, New York, Parkline Chicago Apartments, McDonald’s Corporate Headquarters, Oklahoma City Police Headquarters, and numerous university, hospital, and civic buildings throughout the Midwest, Mid-Atlantic, and Southeast.

ECMS emphasizes its factory certification with major metal manufacturers, extensive customization capacity, and the ability to preserve historic architectural significance. Its Secure-Scan 3D laser scanning service is promoted as a way to reduce project time and cost, while its proprietary panel systems are designed for simplified installation and tested performance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pre-construction services", "3D laser scanning", "Metal panel fabrication", "Custom fabrication services", "Field supervision and installation", "Corporate identity programs", "Historic restoration", "Wet joint MCM panel systems", "Dry joint MCM panel systems", "Formed plate rainscreen systems", "Gravel stop systems", "Architectural metal wall and roof systems"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Metal composite material (MCM)", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Steel", "Stainless steel", "Galvanized steel", "PE/FR core"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Factory certified with all major metal manufacturers", "60,000 sq ft facility with extensive customization capabilities", "Full-service from pre-construction through installation", "Proprietary panel systems (EC-100, EC-150, EC-200, EC-250, EC-300, EC Edge 1000, OVERLY Panel Systems)", "Secure-Scan 3D laser scanning for pre-construction accuracy"], "facts_used": ["Company location: Triadelphia, West Virginia -> db", "60,000 sq ft facility -> /", "Full-service fabrication for engineered architectural metal and exterior envelope systems -> /", "Pre-construction services, 3D laser scanning, metal panel fabrication, fabrication services, field supervision & installation, corporate identity programs, historic restoration -> /services", "Proprietary systems: EC-100, EC-150, EC-200, EC-250, EC-300, EC Edge 1000, OVERLY Panel Systems -> /", "Factory certified with all major metal manufacturers -> /", "Materials: MCM, aluminum, copper, steel, stainless steel, galvan