UPDATE companies SET description='Edesia Nutrition was founded in 2010 in North Kingstown, Rhode Island, by Navyn Salem after she saw a 60 Minutes segment on Plumpy''Nut and recognized the potential to expand its reach. The company operates as a manufacturer of therapeutic foods from its Rhode Island facility, driven by a mission to end malnutrition.

The company produces a full range of ready-to-use therapeutic and supplementary foods, including Plumpy''Nut, at a scale of up to 88 million pounds annually. Its factory sources ingredients from 17 U.S. states and handles formulation, packaging, and quality control for products designed to treat and prevent malnutrition.

