UPDATE companies SET description='Eldor Automotive Powertrain USA operates from Daleville, Virginia, as the American production arm of the Eldor Group, an Italian automotive technology company founded in 1972. The group began in Orsenigo, Italy, producing wound components for radio and television sets before pivoting to automotive ignition systems. The U.S. facility is part of a global network that includes production plants in Italy, China, Turkey, Brazil, and South Korea.

The company manufactures plug-top ignition coils, high-energy ignition systems, and ignition systems for e-fuel and hydrogen applications. Its electrification portfolio includes e-motors, electronic control units, and magnetic components, while its urban e-mobility line covers charging stations and its energy division produces fuel cells. Eldor also designs and develops automated production lines for its own factories, emphasizing a "defect free factory" vision.

