UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Design Technology, Inc. (EDT) was established in 1984 in Sacramento, California, as a certified Small Business Enterprise focused on power distribution equipment and engineering services. The company operates from its headquarters in Sacramento and serves clients across North America and internationally.

EDT supplies low-, medium-, and high-voltage power distribution equipment including transformers, switchgear, motor-control centers, panelboards, equipment buildings, and instrumentation systems. Beyond equipment procurement, the firm provides engineering design, project management, value engineering, technical specification writing, submittal preparation, component list development, field coordination, testing, and integration services. EDT coordinates materials in-house and leverages strategic partnerships with U.S. and international manufacturers to deliver equipment built to customer specifications.

The company serves a diverse set of industries with documented project experience. In data centers, EDT has worked with Apple and Yahoo. For traction power, clients include Honolulu HART, SFMTA, BART, Caltrain, LA Metro, and the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey. Utility customers include SDG&E, HECO, and SMUD. Airport projects cover major New York-area airports. Power generation, municipal water and wastewater, industrial and commercial facilities (California State University campuses, state hospitals, manufacturing plants), ports (Oakland, Long Beach, Bremerton), and government installations such as Vandenberg Air Force Base are also represented.

EDT differentiates itself through its "Power of One" model: a single source for engineering, project management, and equipment acquisition. The company emphasizes unbiased vendor selection — it is not bound by contractual obligations to specific manufacturers — and provides dedicated customer teams that offer direct technical consulting and support throughout a project''s lifetime.', certifications=ARRAY['Small Business Enterprise (SBE)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering design", "Project management", "Equipment procurement", "Value engineering", "Technical specification writing", "Field coordination and testing", "Submittal preparation", "Component list development", "Integration of power distribution equipment", "Turnkey power distribution solutions", "Low-voltage power distribution equipment supply", "Medium-voltage power distribution equipment supply", "High-voltage power distribution equipment supply", "Transformer specification and procurement", "Switchgear specification and procurement", "Motor-control center specification and procurement", "Panelboard specification and procurement", "Equipment building specification and procurement", "Instrumentation system specification and procurement"], "industries": ["Data centers", "Traction power/transit", "Utilities", "Airports", "Power generation", "Municipalities", "Industrial and commercial", "Ports", "Government/military", "Education", "Healthcare"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source engineering, project management, and equipment acquisition", "Unbiased vendor selection without contractual obligations to manufacturers", "Dedicated customer teams for direct technical support", "In-house coordination of materials for proper application", "Value engineering and technical specification writing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 in Sacramento, CA -> /about", "Certified Small Business Enterprise (SBE) -> /about", "Supplies low/medium/high voltage power distribution equipment (transformers, switchgear, MCCs, panelboards, equipment buildings, instrumentation) -> /about", "Provides engineering design, project management, value engineering, technical specification writing, submittals, component lists, field coordination, testing, integration -> /about", "Strategic partnerships with U.S. and international manufacturers; equipment built to user specifications -> /about", "Data center clients: Apple, Yahoo -> /about", "Traction power clients: Honolulu HART, SFMTA, BART, Caltrain, LA Metro, Port Authority NY/NJ, NJ Transit, LIRR -> /about", "Utility clients: SDG&E, HECO, SMUD -> /about", "Airport projects: major NY-area airports -> /about", "Municipal water/wastewater, industrial/commercial (CSU campuses, hospitals, manufacturing) -> /about", "Port clients: Port of Oakland, Port of Long Beach, Bremerton -> /about", "Government: Vandenberg AFB (stainless steel primary substation) -> /about", "Differentiators: single-source ''Power of One'', unbiased vendor selection, dedicated customer teams, in-house material coordination -> /about"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "EDT holds a unique position in the field, as a Value-Added Partner in our customer''s projects. We are not bound by contractual obligations to our vendors which enables us the freedom to choose the highest quality and most appropriate equipment for each project, being unbiased in our choices.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electrical-design-technology-general-switchgear' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Systems of Maine has been operating from Auburn, Maine since 1986. The company was founded with a commitment to quality and customer satisfaction, and over nearly four decades it has grown into a team of project managers, licensed electricians, and technicians. Leadership includes Chief Executive Officer David Tassinari, Chief Financial Officer Mathew Tassinari, and Chief Operations Officer Craig Norcross, supported by division managers across commercial construction, HVAC, and generator sales.

The firm provides a full range of electrical contracting services, including residential and commercial wiring, knob-and-tube remediation, service-entrance upgrades, and 24/7 emergency troubleshooting. It also installs, maintains, and repairs standby generators — both residential and commercial — and offers fuel‑polishing for diesel tanks. A separate HVAC division handles heat‑pump and heating/cooling system installation, repair, and routine maintenance for homes and businesses.

Customers span residential homeowners, commercial property owners, and industrial facilities throughout Maine. The company positions itself as a one‑stop provider for electrical, generator, and HVAC needs across all three sectors.

