UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Applications, Inc. was incorporated in August 1989 in Phoenix, Arizona, by brothers Russell and Robert Churchill. The privately held company began delivering its Watchdog Systems in 1990, focusing on remote monitoring for recreational vehicles and luxury coaches.

The company designs and wholesales a line of remote monitoring equipment that includes tank level, battery, solar charging, generator, and environmental sensors, along with internet-controlled relay outputs. Its IP67-rated controllers are customizable for confined spaces in motor coaches and boats. Products are built to rigid specifications using ISO 9001:2000-certified contract assemblers employing surface-mount technology and automated numeric-controlled handlers. Each Watchdog unit undergoes a 48-hour burn-in, and an in-house systems architect with two decades of mobile-design experience oversees development alongside a network of hardware and software partners.

Electronic Applications sells exclusively to OEM manufacturers and authorized RV and coach service centers; it does not serve the retail market. Its systems are installed in luxury coaches, RVs, remote vacation homes, bunkers, and marine vessels.

The founders established the business to deliver innovative, state-of-the-art monitoring solutions without sacrificing reliability. The firm’s small, agile structure allows it to leverage larger manufacturing partners for economies of scale while maintaining tight control over design, testing, and post-production quality.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design consulting", "Project management", "Remote monitoring system design", "Tank level monitoring", "Battery monitoring", "Solar charging system integration", "Generator monitoring", "Environmental monitoring (temperature, moisture, humidity)", "Internet-controlled relay outputs", "IP67 weather-resistant enclosure design", "Custom firmware/software development", "48-hour burn-in testing", "Surface mount PCB assembly (via certified partners)", "Automated numeric-controlled handling (via partners)", "Built-in diagnostic web interface (E-nostics)"], "industries": ["RV industry", "Luxury coach industry", "Vacation home monitoring", "Bunker monitoring", "Marine industry"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["48-hour burn-in testing on all Watchdog units", "E-nostics built-in diagnostic web interface for remote troubleshooting", "IP67-rated weather-resistant enclosures", "Customizable controllers tailored to OEM requirements", "Wholesale-only distribution through OEMs and authorized service centers"], "facts_used": ["Incorporated August 1989 -> /about", "Founded by brothers Russell and Robert Churchill -> /about", "Privately held company -> /about", "Watchdog Systems since 1990 -> /about", "Headquarters Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Products: tank, battery, solar, generator, environmental monitoring, internet-controlled relays -> /", "IP67 weather-resistant controllers customizable -> /", "Manufactured using ISO 9001:2000 certified circuit assemblers -> /about", "Surface mount technology, automated numeric-controlled handlers -> /about