UPDATE companies SET description='Elemental Energy was founded in 2010 in Portland, Oregon, by graduates of the first accredited Bachelor of Science program in Renewable Energy Engineering. The company is locally owned and operated, with a mission to critically address how society uses and thinks about energy.

The firm designs and installs residential and commercial photovoltaic systems, custom battery storage, and backup power solutions, including Tesla Powerwall and Enphase-based installations. It also provides licensed electrical services for residential, commercial, and industrial projects. With an in-house team of 55 employees, Elemental Energy has completed over 4,000 installations totaling 50 megawatts of capacity across Oregon and southern Washington.

Its customers range from homeowners seeking energy independence and off-grid living to businesses pursuing long-term energy cost savings. The company also serves mobile and remote applications, and partners with the nonprofit Twende Solar to deliver renewable energy to communities in South America, Central America, Africa, and Asia.

Elemental Energy differentiates itself through direct employment of all installers, a 10-year workmanship warranty, and certifications such as NABCEP Certified Installer and Technical Sales Professional, Tesla Powerwall Certified Installer, and Enphase Premium Installer. Its humanitarian outlook and focus on education underpin every project.', certifications=ARRAY['Energy Trust of Oregon Trade Ally','OR CCB 195141','OR Electrical License C1228','WA CCB ELEMEEL823D1','Tesla Powerwall Certified Installer','Enphase Premium Installer']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar PV design and installation", "Commercial solar PV and energy storage design and installation", "Energy storage system design (battery backup)", "Tesla Powerwall installation", "Electrical repairs, upgrades, and installations (residential, commercial, industrial)", "Off-grid system design", "Mobile system installation", "Charitable solar installations (via Twende Solar)", "Site evaluation and assessment", "Permitting and inspection management", "Net metering application assistance"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Non-profit/Charitable", "Off-grid", "Mobile"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall", "Enphase microinverters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house installation team (no subcontractors)", "Tesla Powerwall Certified Installer", "Enphase Premium Installer", "10-year workmanship warranty on installations"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 -> db", "Headquarters Portland, Oregon -> db", "55 employees -> /", "4,000 installations -> /", "50 MW installed -> /", "Founded by graduates of Renewable Energy Engineering program -> /", "Locally owned & operated -> /", "Tesla Powerwall Certified Installer -> /", "Enphase Premium Installer -> /", "NABCEP Certified Installer & Technical Sales Professional -> /about-us", "Energy Trust of Oregon Trade Ally -> /about-us", "OR CCB 195141 -> /", "OR Electrical License C1228