UPDATE companies SET description='EnaChip Inc. operates from Rocky Hill, New Jersey, where it develops high-frequency magnetic components for vertical power delivery in AI data centers.

The company designs and fabricates bespoke magnetics that enable integrated voltage regulator (IVR) and transverse inductor voltage regulator (TLVR) topologies. Its core technology relies on an electroplated core stack with thick copper planar windings and high-flux-density magnetic materials, all processed on standard semiconductor equipment. The resulting components achieve low DC and AC resistance, support switching frequencies above 10 MHz, and fit within sub-millimeter, wafer-level packages that can be placed at the board, package, or die level.

Its magnetics are designed to integrate with gallium nitride (GaN) and advanced silicon switches, targeting the last few centimeters of power delivery where conversion losses are highest. The company also lists energy harvesting and energy conversion among its served markets.

EnaChip states that its differentiation lies in co-designing power, signal, sensing, and actuation functions rather than stitching together disconnected parts. By electroplating on standard semiconductor lines, the company says it dramatically reduces manufacturing time while delivering magnetics that suppress core loss at high frequencies, enabling low-inductance designs that drop into any level of the design stack.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrochemical wafer fabrication", "Wafer-aligned fabrication", "Electroplated magnetic core fabrication", "Thick copper planar winding", "High-flux-density material integration", "Low-loss magnetic material processing", "High-frequency switching magnetics (above 10 MHz)", "IVR/TLVR magnetics design", "Custom geometry magnetic components", "Wafer-level array manufacturing"], "industries": ["AI data centers", "High-performance computing", "Power electronics", "Energy harvesting", "Energy conversion"], "materials": ["Copper", "High-flux-density magnetic materials", "Low-loss magnetic materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Electroplated core stack with thick copper planar windings", "High-flux-density materials for strong current handling in a small core", "Low-loss magnetic materials for efficient switching above 10 MHz", "Electroplating on standard semiconductor equipment cuts manufacturing time", "Components drop into board, package, or die level designs"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Rocky Hill, New Jersey -> db", "Develops magnetics for AI data centers -> /", "Uses electroplated core stack with thick copper planar windings -> /", "Electroplating on standard semiconductor equipment -> /", "Targets 800V DC architectures -> /", "Offers wafer-level array devices -> /", "Integrates with GaN and advanced silicon switches -> /", "Custom geometries, feature sets, layer counts -> /", "Capabilities include electrochemical wafer fabrication -> db", "Capabilities include wafer-aligned fabrication -> db", "Industries served include Energy Harvesting -> db", "Industries served include Energy conversion -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our bespoke magnetics unlock IVR and TLVR designs, built for the future of power delivery.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='enachip-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Encompass Manufacturing operates from Cookeville, Tennessee. The company traces its roots back over 35 years, originally founded as Putnam County Plastic Molding by Ricky Sherrell. Today it is certified as a Women''s Business Enterprise through WBENC, with Samantha Sherrell serving as president and Ricky Sherrell as vice president.

The company specializes in plastic injection molding supported by a full-service tool shop that handles prototyping, in-house maintenance, and engineering modifications. Its press lineup ranges from 125 to 1,214 tons, enabling a broad spectrum of part sizes. Beyond molding, Encompass offers secondary operations including sonic welding, hot stamping, screen and pad printing, insert molding, vibratory welding, drilling, assembly, and a suite of metrology and material analysis services. A Mattec/MVP monitoring system provides real-time production data and preventive maintenance tracking.

Customers range from small startups to major automotive suppliers worldwide. The quality system, certified to ISO 9001, supports APQP, PPAP, ISIR, and full traceability from raw material through final assembly, all managed through a customized ERP platform.

