UPDATE companies SET description='Enercon Engineering LLC, based in East Peoria, Illinois, traces its roots back over four decades to a 5,000-square-foot garage. The company was acquired by Generac Holdings Inc. in April 2026, becoming a subsidiary of the global energy technology leader.

Today Enercon designs and manufactures precision-engineered low- and medium-voltage switchgear (up to 15 kV), industrial control panels, generator docking stations, sound-attenuated enclosures, and mobile power packaging systems. Operations span a 160,000-square-foot facility that includes a 50,000-square-foot electrical assembly area with client-specific production lines, an in-house sheet metal fabrication shop, a military-standard paint booth, and on-site load-testing capacity for generation systems up to 2.5 MW. The company reports more than 50,000 completed projects deployed across 110 countries and has added capacity for an additional 1,000-plus docking stations per year.

Customers include data-center operators, defense and military programs, utilities, hospitals, correctional facilities, and industrial manufacturers. Named references feature Temple University, Waupaca Foundry, the Hampden County Sheriff’s Department, Renaissance, Gen-Alliance, and Oberlander Electric Company.

Enercon emphasizes vertically integrated, engineering-driven manufacturing — handling design, fabrication, integration, PLC/HMI programming, and full functional and load testing in house to UL 891, UL 1558, UL 508A, and MIL-SPEC standards. The firm says this end-to-end control ensures dependable, field-proven power solutions built to perform in extreme environments from -40 °C to +50 °C.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 891','UL 508A','UL 1558','UL Listed - Circuit Breaker and Metal-Clad Switchgear over 600 Volts','ISO 9001:2015','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical engineering (power distribution design, control logic, system layout, compliance documentation)", "Mechanical engineering (enclosure design, cable management, structural layout, thermal management)", "Custom metal fabrication (sheet metal parts, structural frames, enclosures, skids, brackets)", "System integration (electrical and mechanical assembly, routing, connection, communication validation)", "PLC & HMI programming (Allen-Bradley, Siemens, Schneider Electric, GE platforms)", "Testing & validation (functional testing, load testing, string testing, UL/MIL-SPEC/custom standards)", "Contract manufacturing (build-to-print, value-added design, single builds to long-term production)", "Field service & on-site support (commissioning, retrofits, upgrades, emergency repairs, nationwide)", "Parts support (spare/replacement parts, obsolete component replacement, fabrication and sourcing)", "Switchgear and controls manufacturing (low/medium voltage up to 15kV)", "Industrial control panel manufacturing (UL 508A, UL 698A)", "Generator docking station manufacturing (400-4000 amp)", "Generator enclosure manufacturing (sound-attenuated)", "Mobile power packaging", "Tactical electric power systems", "Power upgrades and retrofits", "Rapid power solutions manufacturing", "Critical resource expertise"], "industries": ["Data centers", "Defense and military operations", "Utilities", "Healthcare (hospitals)", 