on, we design and manufacture precision-engineered switchgear, control panels, generator docking stations, and power packaging systems", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='enercon-engineering-llc-a-generac-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Energy Select operates from Leonardtown in Southern Maryland, with a second office in Western Maryland. The company was founded in Southern Maryland, though no specific year is disclosed in public materials, and ownership structure is not stated.

The firm provides turnkey energy solutions including custom solar photovoltaic system design and installation for residential and commercial clients, battery backup storage, energy-efficient LED lighting retrofits, electric vehicle charger installation, and comprehensive energy analysis. They install Enphase microinverter systems and coordinate with the local utility SMECO to secure rebates for insulation and efficiency upgrades. As a member-owner of the Amicus Solar Cooperative, they collaborate with a national network of independent solar companies.

Energy Select serves homeowners, businesses, and commercial property owners throughout Maryland. Residential customers include owners of historic homes such as a 1927 cottage on Cobb Island. Commercial clients seek LED lighting upgrades, EV charging infrastructure, and backup power systems. The company also performs commercial electrical work.

The company positions itself as a local, full-service energy partner that guides clients through every step of their solar journey, emphasizing energy independence, cost reduction, and carbon footprint reduction. Membership in the Amicus Solar Cooperative is cited as a way to strengthen their ability to serve customers and communities through collaboration.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design and installation", "Battery backup system installation", "Commercial LED lighting retrofits", "Electric vehicle charger installation", "Energy analysis and auditing", "Commercial electrical work", "Utility rebate coordination (SMECO)"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Energy efficiency", "Electric vehicle infrastructure", "Commercial electrical contracting"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Enphase microinverter systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Member-owner of Amicus Solar Cooperative", "Utility rebate coordination with SMECO", "Full-service energy solutions under one roof", "Local presence in Southern and Western Maryland"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Leonardtown, Maryland -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "Second office in Western Maryland -> db (description)", "Services: solar, battery, LED lighting, EV charging, energy analysis -> / (Our Services section)", "Installs Enphase systems -> / (review by Harlan Higgins)", "Works with SMECO for rebates -> / (review by Amy James)", "Member of Amicus Solar Cooperative -> / (Our Impact section)", "Serves residential and commercial customers -> / (Service Needed dropdown in quote form)", "Performs commercial electrical work -> / (Service Needed dropdown)", "Company type is installer/service -> / (homepage title ''Maryland Solar Installers'' and review content)"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Homepage title ''Maryland Solar Installers'' and review s