UPDATE companies SET description='Engineered Equipment Company (EEC) was established in Anchorage, Alaska, in 1967 by Richard (Dick) W. Spils, an engineer with Standard Oil who saw a need for a local representative to serve industrial product manufacturers in the state. The company has maintained continuous operations in Alaska since its founding. In 1994, J. Mark Wilson acquired the business and expanded its reach, opening a branch office in Bothell, Washington, in 2016 to cover the broader Northwest region.

EEC operates as a manufacturer''s representative and distributor of electrical products and process measurement and control equipment. Its product portfolio includes electrical equipment, valves, pumps, and instrumentation from manufacturers. The company takes a consultative approach, working with customers to solve complex technical applications across industrial and heavy commercial markets. With offices in Anchorage and Bothell, EEC serves Alaska, Washington, Oregon, and Idaho.

The company''s customer base spans process plants and large-scale commercial installations in industries such as power generation, water and wastewater, oil and gas, food and beverage, chemical, pulp and paper, semiconductor, life sciences, higher education, health care, transportation, and infrastructure.

EEC distinguishes itself as the longest-operating manufacturer''s representative of process control and electrical equipment in Alaska. The firm emphasizes a combination of responsiveness and demonstrated technical competence to earn customer trust.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Manufacturer''s representation", "Distribution of electrical equipment", "Distribution of valves", "Distribution of pumps", "Distribution of instrumentation products", "Technical consultation for industrial applications"], "industries": ["Power generation", "Water and wastewater", "Oil and gas", "Food and beverage", "Chemical", "Pulp and paper", "Semiconductor", "Life sciences", "Higher education", "Health care", "Transportation", "Infrastructure", "Industrial markets", "Heavy commercial markets"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Longest-operating manufacturer''s representative of process control and electrical equipment in Alaska", "Consultative approach to solving complex technical applications", "Responsive service backed by demonstrated technical competence", "Offices in Anchorage and Bothell covering Alaska, Washington, Oregon, and Idaho", "Represents leading manufacturers of industrial process control and electrical products"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1967 by Richard (Dick) W. Spils in Anchorage, Alaska -> /about-us", "Purchased by J. Mark Wilson in 1994 -> /about-us", "Expanded to Bothell, WA office in 2016 -> /about-us", "Manufacturer''s representative and distributor of electrical products and process measurement and control equipment -> /", "Serves Alaska, Washington, Oregon, Idaho -> /", "Industries served: power generation, water & wastewater, oil & gas, food & beverage, chemical, pulp & paper, semiconductor, life sciences, higher education, health care, transportation, infrastructure -> /", "Consultative approach, responsive with technical competence -> /about-us", "Longest operating