UPDATE companies SET description='Engineered Plastic Components (EPC Manufacturing) is headquartered in Lebanon, Kentucky, and operates a network of 21 manufacturing facilities across the United States, Canada, and Mexico. The company serves as a Tier 1 supplier to automotive OEMs and provides precision-engineered plastic components for appliance, medical device, and consumer product markets.

The company runs injection molding presses ranging from 25 to 4,400 tons, enabling production of small precision parts up to large automotive components. Core processes include two-shot molding, overmolding, insert molding, gas assist, and in-mold decoration. Secondary operations encompass hot stamping, pad printing, heat transfer, silk screening, heat staking, and multiple welding technologies (sonic, spin, vibration, hot plate, ultrasonic, orbital). Facilities also offer painting (1K/2K/waterborne), powder coating, metal stamping, cleanroom manufacturing, leak testing, and full assembly and sub-assembly. The Lebanon, Kentucky plant spans 250,000 square feet and operates 24/7; the Bellevue, Ohio facility covers 192,000 square feet with 71 presses; other sites range from 52,500 to 150,000 square feet.

EPC supplies complex instrument panel assemblies, interior and exterior trim with Class-A finishes, and painted components to major automotive OEMs. For appliance manufacturers, it produces control panels, structural housings, and components with UV stability and heat resistance. Medical device customers receive FDA-compliant cleanroom-molded surgical instrument components and diagnostic equipment housings made from sterilizable materials. Consumer product lines include electronics housings, protective cases, and appliance parts with emphasis on durability and aesthetics.

The company emphasizes its North American footprint, IATF 16949 and ISO 13485 certifications, and in-house metrology (CMM, vision, DSC) as differentiators. It also highlights environmentally conscious manufacturing using recycled materials and sustainable practices, along with a certified minority-owned facility in Osceola, Wisconsin that provides engineering, tooling support, and mold repair.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (25-4,400 ton)", "Two-shot molding", "Overmolding", "Insert molding", "Gas assist molding", "In-mold decoration", "Hot stamping", "Pad printing", "Heat transfer", "Silk screening", "Heat staking", "Sonic welding", "Spin welding", "Vibration welding", "Hot plate welding", "Ultrasonic welding", "Orbital welding", "Leak testing", "Assembly", "Sub-assembly", "Painting (1K/2K/Waterborne)", "Powder coating", "Metal stamping", "Cleanroom manufacturing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Appliances", "Medical Devices", "Consumer Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses (20-4,400 ton)", "Paint lines (1K/2K/Waterborne)", "CMM", "Vision systems", "DSC", "Ultrasonic welding equipment", "Orbital welding equipment", "Leak testing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["21 manufacturing facilities across 3 countries (US, Canada, Mexico)", "24/7 production capability at multiple sites", "Injection molding range from 25 to 4,400 tons", "IATF 16949 and ISO 13485 certified facilities with cleanroom manufacturing", "In-house metrology lab with CMM, vision systems, and DSC"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lebanon, Kentucky -> db", "21 manufacturing facilities across 3 countries -> homepage /", "24/7 production capability -> homepage /", "Injection molding range 25-4,400 tons -> homepage /", "IATF 16949, ISO 9001, ISO 14001, ISO 13485 certifications -> db certifications and facility pages", "Facility sizes: 250,000 sq ft (Lebanon), 192,000 sq ft (Bellevue), 150,000 sq ft (Ormond Beach, Stratford), 145,000 sq ft (Columbia), 125,000 sq ft (Grinnell), 73,000 sq ft (Osceola), 52,500 sq ft (Anderson) -> facility pages", "Automotive: instrument panel assemblies, interior/exterior trim, paint capabilities -> homepage /", "Appliances: control panels, housings, structural components -> homepage /", "Medical: cleanroom manufacturing, surgical components, diagnostic housings -> homepage /", "Consumer: electronics housings, appliance parts, protective cases -> homepage /", "Certified Minority Supplier at Osceola, WI -> facility page", "In-house metrology lab (CMM, Vision, DSC) -> Anderson facility page", "Paint lines (1K/2K/Waterborne) -> Ormond Beach facility page", "Metal stamping -> Ormond Beach and Stratford facility pages", "Cleanroom manufacturing for medical devices -> Osceola facility page", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation -> Osceola facility page", "Engineering and tooling support, mold repair -> Osceola facility page", "Environmentally conscious manufacturing with recycled materials -> homepage /", "Strategic North American coverage -> homepage /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a trusted Tier 1 Supplier, we manufacture complex automotive components including instrument panel assemblies, interior and exterior trim including paint capabilities for major OEMs across North America.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='engineered-plastic-components' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ennis Fine Furniture was founded in 1946 in Boise, Idaho, by Cecil Ennis and his brother-in-law after they returned from World War II. The pair purchased a former horse stable at 23rd Street and Fairview Avenue, remodeled it, and began selling furniture and appliances. The business remains family-owned, now led by the founder''s grandchildren Rick, Jeff, and Cathy.

The company operates two showrooms — one in Boise at 275 S 23rd Street and another in Spokane, Washington — offering living room, bedroom, and dining room collections that include sofas, sectionals, beds, dressers, tables, and case goods. Ennis Fine Furniture positions itself as a destination for semi-custom and luxury furnishings, providing design consultation, custom finish selection, delivery, installation, and haul-away of old furniture.

The retailer serves homeowners throughout the Pacific Northwest, with customers citing purchases of dining sets, lighting, upholstery, and accessories. Testimonials highlight the firm''s design assistance and personalized service, though no commercial or contract clients are mentioned in the available materials.

Ennis Fine Furniture emphasizes its multi-generational legacy and community roots as its differentiator, stating that clients become "part of our family" and that each purchase represents "a piece of history, a touch of artistry, and a home that tells your story."', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture retail sales", "Custom finish and detailing selection", "Interior design consultation", "Delivery and installation", "Old furniture removal"], "industries": ["Residential furniture retail", "Home furnishings", "Interior design services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 by Cecil Ennis and brother-in-law -> /about-us", "Family-owned, now run by grandchildren Rick, Jeff, Cathy -> /about-us", "Two showrooms: Boise (275 S 23rd St) and Spokane (8313 N Division St) -> /about-us", "Sells living room, bedroom, dining room furniture -> /", "Offers semi-custom and luxury furnishings -> /about-us", "Provides design consultation, delivery, installation, haul-away -> /", "Serves homeowners across the Northwest -> /about-us", "Emphasizes family legacy and personalized experience -> /about-us", "Founded year 1946 from database -> db", "Headquarters Boise, Idaho from database -> db"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Visit Our Boise Showroom: 275 S 23rd Street, Boise, ID 83702", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ennis-fine-furniture-boise' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Epic Welding & Mfg is a full-service welding and fabrication shop based in West Fargo, North Dakota. The company has been operating for over 20 years, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The shop provides a range of metal fabrication services under one roof, including MIG welding up to 450 amps, stick welding up to 400 amps, TIG welding, CNC plasma cutting of mild steel up to one inch thick, 12-foot press brake forming, plate shearing up to 1/4-inch by 10 feet, sawing with an 18-inch by 18-inch capacity, punching, notching, sand blasting, and epoxy painting using an automated two-part paint blender. It also offers assembly for industrial and agricultural equipment. Production runs span from single prototypes to batches of up to 1,000 pieces, with common outputs such as trailers, agricultural equipment, and pipe work.

