UPDATE companies SET description='EverGreen Treated Wood, doing business as Iowa Wood Preservers, operates from its headquarters in Oskaloosa, Iowa, with additional facilities in Sutton, Nebraska, and Willmar, Minnesota. The company is family-owned and was founded by Vic Sowl, who remains listed as founder; his son Nick Sowl serves as president. The business began as a wholesale supplier of pressure-treated lumber and has expanded to three Midwestern locations serving regional markets.

The company pressure-treats and manufactures a range of lumber products for structural and specialty applications. Its treatment lines include CCA for commercial, industrial, and agricultural uses; MCA-based Lifewood Residential for exterior exposure; and Pyro-Guard fire-retardant lumber and plywood for enclosed structural applications. Value-added services include kiln drying after treatment (KDAT) to improve stability and allow immediate finishing, precision end trimming to uniform lengths, notched runner fabrication for shed foundations, and V-groove paneling for interior wall and ceiling use.

EverGreen serves agricultural, residential, government and utility, marine, and wood-foundation construction markets. Residential buyers specify Lifewood for decks, framing, and guardrails. Government and utility projects call for fire-retardant and marine-grade plywood, while wood-foundation systems rely on pressure-treated lumber for below-grade durability.

