UPDATE companies SET description='FAT ENZO, Inc. operates from Monroe, Connecticut, where it was incorporated in January 2009. The business is family‑owned and operated, founded by Robert Vincent Piccirillo (CEO), Matthew Anthony Piazza (CCO, deceased 2019), and Joan Karen Iannotti (CFO, deceased 2021), with their dog Enzo serving as the brand’s namesake and mascot. The venture began as a creative outlet for the founders’ passion for music and design, quickly evolving into a full‑service garment decoration shop.

The company provides custom screen printing, embroidery, graphic design, illustration, logo creation, color separation, vectorization, and digitization, all performed in‑house at its Monroe facility. Products decorated include t‑shirts, caps, totes, polos, hoodies, and uniforms. No facility square footage or headcount figures are disclosed.

FAT ENZO serves a broad clientele summarized as the “Three B’s”: bands, brands, and businesses. Concrete customer types listed include for‑profit and non‑profit companies, corporations, mom‑and‑pop shops, religious organizations, social clubs, college fraternities and sororities, sports teams (including bowling, darts, and roller derby), motorcycle clubs, and political candidates or PACs. The shop ships throughout the Northeast (CT, VT, RI, MA, NY, NJ) and Florida, with nationwide fulfillment available.

